# Template. Copy to secrets.sops.env, fill in, encrypt:
#
#   cp secrets.sops.env.example secrets.sops.env
#   $EDITOR secrets.sops.env
#   sops -e -i secrets.sops.env
#
# Two kinds of line, neither of them a value: identifying values, and `pass://` references that
# `pass-cli run` resolves once `sops exec-env` has loaded this file into the environment. No
# braces — `run` resolves bare URIs and ignores braced ones, the inverse of `inject`. See
# .just/tofu.just and docs/src/tofu/index.md.
#
# TAILSCALE_TAILNET is deliberately absent: Ansible owns the tailnet suffix, so this module reads
# it via refs.env. Naming it here would override the ref and reintroduce the second copy.

# The policy-file OAuth client: write on the tailnet ACL, and deliberately neither of the two
# key-minting clients — ansible/roles/tailscale's (config/secrets.sops.yaml) or the Kubernetes
# operator's (Infisical /infra/tailscale). No two need the same scope, so they stay separate.
TAILSCALE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=pass://futharkd/tailscale-policy/client id
TAILSCALE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=pass://futharkd/tailscale-policy/client secret
